From b464c55d293ba87e4c33a6d4a6c58aa2964378ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raimondas Lencevicius <59739769+raimondasl@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:40:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05/17] Add payload snapshot tests for Gemini 3.8 Flash high
 runs

Runs BenchmarkingAgent.main() on a scripted game through the real
google-genai SDK over httpx.MockTransport and compares the full JSON body
of every Interactions request with a literal snapshot:

- google-gemini-3-8-flash-high: carry-forward sentence in the system
  instruction; only visible user/model text is sent, never thought items,
  signatures or reasoning summaries; the oldest turn pair is dropped above
  MAX_CONTEXT_LENGTH; provider usage above 175k never compacts.
- the same profile with agent.carry_forward_instruction=false: identical
  requests except the system instruction, which then equals the Provider
  Adapter's; the flag also wins over analysis_mode.
- google-gemini-3-8-flash-high-provider-adapter: signed thought steps
  and model outputs are replayed exactly as parsed; at 175k the harness
  summary request (8,192-token cap) sees the full native history, and
  later turns restart from the user-role bridge.
- every request uses thinking_level=high and thinking_summaries=auto;
  service_tier is absent by default and sent on every request, including
  the summary request, when configured.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
